  "comment": "Core i7 Max. CPU clock rate 1.6 GHz to 3.47 GHz Intel Core i7 is Intel 's brand name for several families of desktop and laptop 64-bit x86-64 processors using the Intel Nehalem microarchitecture . It is a successor to the Intel Core 2 brand. Prior to 2010, all models were quad-core processors. In 2010, the name was applied to dual-core Arrandale models, and the upcoming Gulftown Core i7-9x0X",
